WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.570
- [Narrator] In the heart of Mexico City

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:05.646
is a school exclusively
for gifted children.

00:00:05.646 --> 00:00:06.479
(whooshes)

00:00:06.479 --> 00:00:07.800
And at the heart of that school

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.895
is a gifted 16-year-old prodigy,

00:00:09.895 --> 00:00:10.728
(whooshes)

00:00:10.728 --> 00:00:15.603
named Dafne Almazán.

00:00:17.825 --> 00:00:20.575
(cheerful music)

00:00:24.671 --> 00:00:27.115
(playing piano)

00:00:27.115 --> 00:00:29.010
- [Narrator] Dafne is a child prodigy

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.740
who became the world's
youngest psychologist

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.370
at the age of 13,

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:33.760
and Forbes Magazine named her

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.450
one of Mexico's most powerful women.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:37.283
(paper crinkles)

00:00:37.283 --> 00:00:40.100
At 14, she received her
masters in education,

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.854
and right now, she is
finishing a doctorate in law.

00:00:43.854 --> 00:00:44.687
(whooshes)

00:00:44.687 --> 00:00:46.230
As if that wasn't enough,

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:49.980
Dafne speaks English,
French, Latin and Mandarin,

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:52.940
and finds time during the
day to study them all.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.780
Did I say that she's only 16?

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:55.663
- Yes, you did.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:57.740
- [Narrator] It is estimated that there is

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.330
over one million gifted
children in Mexico,

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:02.430
with a talent waiting to be tapped.

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.090
So Dafne is committed to nurturing

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:06.790
the vast talent of the
gifted children of Mexico.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:08.840
That's why she teaches psychology

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.200
at the school she once graduated from,

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.889
Centro de Atención al Talento.

00:01:13.889 --> 00:01:17.056
(upbeat string music)

00:01:34.387 --> 00:01:37.054
(playing piano)

00:01:44.157 --> 00:01:45.523
(upbeat guitar music)

00:01:45.523 --> 00:01:47.690
(exhales)

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:50.934
(thuds)

00:01:56.066 --> 00:01:57.440
(punches)

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:59.120
- [Narrator] For example,
there's this science whiz kid

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:00.620
who knows the entire periodic table

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:01.920
like the back of his hand.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.550
- [Narrator] Or this
kid, with a sharp memory

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:09.803
that allows him to memorize
every bone in the human body.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.040
- [Narrator] There is this 6-year-old kid

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:14.903
presenting on an interesting subject.

00:02:29.276 --> 00:02:32.943
(majestic orchestral music)

00:02:47.903 --> 00:02:50.486
(tonal music)

